From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:16:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] A chunk keeps no arrays it has not needed, and a template's
 worlds share its heights and biomes

The entity counts, the bucket index and its pads were ten arrays, 0.7 KB, for
every chunk, and most of a map's chunks never hold an entity: they are the
shared, never written empty ones until the first entity enters. A player chunk
makes its list of changed blocks with the first change.

A chunk read from a template's store takes the heights and biomes another
world on that template already holds for it, 1.3 KB a chunk that every world
read into arrays of its own. They are held weakly by the store, as the
packets are. The first write in a world - a relight, a biome set, any caller of
getHeightMap or getBiomeIndex, which may write - gives that world's chunk
arrays of its own; the readers in the server read them through athenaHeights
and athenaBiomes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

